      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Settled by Mormon pioneers in 1864, Bennington was officially organized as a church branch in 1866 and became the Bennington Ward in 1877.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        9,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bennington_idaho",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The valley’s microclimate moderates weather but brings persistent fog and frost in winter and early spring, thanks to cold air drainage and lake influences.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bennington_idaho",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early settlers moved the townsite in 1873 to its current spot near Bennington Creek after harsh winters revealed the original location’s challenges.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bennington_idaho",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Bennington’s fertile land, fed by the Bear River and Bear Lake, supports a short growing season that ends with early autumn chills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
